; BENZ.itp -- benzene cosolvent probe (CGenFF standard residue BENZ, C6H6)
; SOURCE (read + re-verified on ARCC 2026-07-22): GROMACS CHARMM36-jul2021 port
;   the CHARMM36 (July 2021) GROMACS force-field distribution
;   residue  BENZ            : cgenff.rtp line 8256  ("; C6H6, benzene, adm jr.")
;   atom types HGR61/CG2R61  : ffnonbonded.itp lines 185 / 218
;   bond   CG2R61-CG2R61     : ffbonded.itp line 515  (b0 0.13750 nm, Kb 255224.00)
;   bond   CG2R61-HGR61      : ffbonded.itp line 554  (b0 0.10800 nm, Kb 284512.00)
;   angle  CG2R61-CG2R61-CG2R61 : ffbonded.itp line 3030 (120, 334.720, ub 0.24162, Kub 29288.00)
;   angle  CG2R61-CG2R61-HGR61  : ffbonded.itp line 3070 (120, 251.040, ub 0.21525, Kub 18409.60)
;   dih    CG2R61-CG2R61-CG2R61-CG2R61 : ffbonded.itp line 12073 (180, 12.970400, mult 2)
;   dih    CG2R61-CG2R61-CG2R61-HGR61  : ffbonded.itp line 12112 (180, 17.572800, mult 2)
;   dih    HGR61-CG2R61-CG2R61-HGR61   : ffbonded.itp line 12222 (180, 10.041600, mult 2)
;
; All bonded params are INLINED (explicit funct+values) so this file is self-contained
; and needs NO CGenFF [bondtypes]/[angletypes]/[dihedraltypes] from the campaign FF.
; PREREQUISITE: toppar/BENZ_atomtypes.itp (defines CG2R61/HGR61) MUST be #included after
;   toppar/forcefield.itp and BEFORE this file -- the campaign forcefield.itp does NOT
;   define these two aromatic types (grep-verified empty 2026-07-22).
; This file intentionally contains NO [ atomtypes ] block (it would be "defined too late"
;   after a [moleculetype]) and NO [ position_restraints ] block (benzene must stay
;   UNRESTRAINED so it can diffuse/partition from t=0 under -DPOSRES).
; nrexcl 3 + campaign [defaults] gen-pairs=yes,fudgeLJ=1.0,fudgeQQ=1.0 -> [pairs] 1-4 auto-generated.

[ moleculetype ]
